At the cathode, aluminium ions gain electrons:


Al^{3++3e⁻→ Al}


At the anode, oxide ions lose electrons:


2O^{2-→ O₂+4e⁻}


Option A incorrectly places electrons among the products of the cathode reaction. Option C puts electrons on the wrong side of the anode equation.

